## Verdict: not freezable

Four findings are resolved; three remain partial. No finding is wholly unaddressed, but the remaining attestation and fail-closed gaps are freeze blockers.

| # | Status | Current-code evidence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **PARTIAL** | The runner now requires the correct gate, literal `passed is True`, a nonempty roster, the full current environment fingerprint, and frozen SHAs: [run_generalization_ls.py:34](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/run_generalization_ls.py:34), [run_generalization_ls.py:42](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/run_generalization_ls.py:42), [run_generalization_ls.py:54](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/run_generalization_ls.py:54). It still accepts any nonempty roster. Replay permits arbitrary `--count` or `--stars` at [replay_gate.py:159](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/replay_gate.py:159), while the pass predicate checks only no mismatches plus one strict-v2 result at [replay_gate.py:214](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/replay_gate.py:214). No 928-count, uniqueness, or roster digest is enforced. |
| 2 | **PARTIAL** | Final campaign SHAs are now present in the D2 summary, D3 report, runner, panels, and metrics—for example [build_d2_shards.py:314](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:314), [build_d3_roster.py:218](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d3_roster.py:218), and [metrics_generalization.py:680](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py:680). Replay still omits campaign SHAs from its report at [replay_gate.py:216](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/replay_gate.py:216), and the panel gate records only environment at [panel_golden_gate.py:150](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:150). No stage takes initial and final snapshots or fails if campaign code changes mid-stage. |
| 3 | **PARTIAL** | Control IDs now use the sorted fixed template pool at [build_d2_shards.py:177](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:177), and every arm-B row carries `control_campaign_id` at [build_d2_shards.py:246](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:246). Result reuse is additionally bound to shard and environment hashes at [run_generalization_ls.py:104](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/run_generalization_ls.py:104). However, the builder reuses an existing directory without rejecting extras at [build_d2_shards.py:170](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:170), and the runner executes every `*.csv.gz`, rather than the manifest’s exact set, at [run_generalization_ls.py:110](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/run_generalization_ls.py:110). |
| 4 | **RESOLVED** | Actual retained modes and rejected modes are captured per campaign at [build_d2_shards.py:227](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:227) and written at [build_d2_shards.py:292](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:292). Metrics reads `injected_modes.csv` exclusively at [metrics_generalization.py:240](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py:240). Unique target-mode rejection accounting is separate at [build_d2_shards.py:294](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:294). |
